  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Let's put the two stops together."
   ],
   [
    2.096,
    "A gene in the nucleus is copied into messenger RNA."
   ],
   [
    5.82,
    "The messenger leaves through a nuclear pore."
   ],
   [
    8.333,
    "Meanwhile, in the nucleolus, rRNA and proteins have been built into ribosome subunits, and those left through the pores too."
   ],
   [
    16.693,
    "In the cytoplasm, the two subunits clamp onto the messenger."
   ],
   [
    20.885,
    "If the ribosome floats free, the protein is made in the cytosol, and it works there."
   ],
   [
    26.393,
    "If the ribosome sits on the rough endoplasmic reticulum, the protein is mostly bound for a membrane, or for export from the cell."
   ],
   [
    34.753,
    "Lesson three follows that road."
   ],
   [
    36.888,
    "Same ribosome, different place."
   ]
